E2. SYED RAFIULLAII to move that the proposed amendments in the Rules of Procedure andConduct ofBusiness in the National Assembly, 2007, be adoptedRESOLUIIONS
83. MR. ANJUM AQEEL KIIAN to move the following resolution:-"This House is ofthe opinion that the Government should take immediate steps to provide compensation toaffeotees whose land have been acquired by the CDA in sector E-12, C-13, C-14, C-15, C-16 and H-16,Islamabad.E4, MS. SHAHIDA REHMANI to move the following resolution:-"This House is of the opinion that the Government should take immediate steps to dualize the northembypass in Karachi, which links Balochistan and Karachi Port.E5. SYED RAFITILLAII to move the following resolution:-"This House is of the opinion that the Govemment should take immediate steps to halt tax evasion whichdrains hundreds ofbillions rupees ofpublic revenue and also undermines national development.E6. SAIIIBZADA SIBGHATULLAII to move the following resolution:-"This House is of the opinion that the Govemment should take immediate steps to provide natural gas toUpper Dir.
E7. MR. CHANGAZE AIIMAD KIIAN
to move the following resolution:-
"This House is of the opinion that the Govemment should take immediate steps to complete the greenenclave phase-I housing authority project and also ensure possession of plots to genuine allottees on merit.
MOTIONS UI{DERRULE 259
8E. MR. ALI MUIIAMMAD KIIAII to move the following motion:-"This House may discuss the situation arising out ofincrease in the prices ofpetroleum products.89. DR. STIARMILA FARUQUI to move the following motion:-"This House may discuss the performance ofPakistan National Shipping Corporation (PNSC).90. SYED RAFIULLAH to move the following motion:-"This House may discuss the climate change policy of the Govemment.91. MS. ALIYA KAMRAN to move the following motion:-"This House may discuss the performance of Electricity Distribution Companies (DISCOs).92. MS, SHAHIDA REHMAM to move the following motion:-"This House may discuss the domestic violence against women in the country.DISCUSSION ON MATTER OF URGENT PUBLIC IMPORTANCE I,]IIDER RIJLE E7
93. MR. FATEII ULLAII KIIAN "to discuss a matter of urgentpublic importance regarding allocation of 46 million rupees by the Prime Minister for the relief andrehabilitation for the Dera Ismail Khan flood affected communities".
MATTERS OTIIER THAAI POINTS OF ORDER
94.
Raising matters under Rule 18 which are not Points ofOrder.CALLING ATTENTION NOTICE
95. MS. NAEEMA KISHWER KHAN MS. ALIYAKAMRANMR. ]\{ISBAH IIDDIN MS. SHAHIDA BEGIIM to invite attention of theMinister for Finance and Revenue, to a matter ofurgent public importance regarding proposal to withdrawtax and duty exemptions for erstwhile FATA and PATA regions, causing grave concem amongst the public.
